  "thig14.1:18.1": "",
  "thig14.1:18.2": "The <i lang='pi' translate='no'>dassane</i> (plural) are seen by him, so they must be the “eyes”. | In this poem, the English word “eye” must serve for five Pali words: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>cakkhu</i>, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>locana</i>, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>akkhi</i>, and <i lang='pi' translate='no'>dassana</i> are all from roots of “seeing”, while <i lang='pi' translate='no'>nayana</i> is from the root sense “leading”. ",
